course: dictionary
lesson: 15384
title: Saying exactly what you mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To specify something means to say or write it clearly and exactly, so nobody has to guess. «Please specify your size on the form.» The form wants one exact answer, such as medium or size 8, not «a sort of big one». The clues are please, form and size.
explain: Specify also has a formal meaning: to state something as a rule or requirement. «Unless otherwise specified, homework is due on Friday.» This means Friday is the rule, unless a different rule has been written down.
explain: Ask yourself: is the writer asking for an exact detail? If yes, specify means giving that detail precisely.
fact: Specify is a verb: specify, specifies, specified, specifying.
fact: «Specify» means to say or write something clearly and exactly.
fact: «Specify exactly» means giving the precise detail, not a rough guess.
fact: «Unless otherwise specified» means unless a different rule has been stated.
fact: A good check is to swap in «say exactly» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Please specify the date you want to visit.» What does specify mean here? | Forget the date | *Say exactly which date | Guess a date that is roughly right | Draw a picture of a calendar
exercise: The teacher writes, «Unless otherwise specified, write in pen.» What does specified suggest? | Crossed out | Written in pencil only | *Stated as a rule | Forgotten completely
exercise: Ben ___ the time and place for the party, so everyone knows exactly where to go. Which word fits best? | specify | specified | specifying | *specifies
test: «Please specify your favourite colour.» What must you do? | Sing a song about it | *Give one exact answer | Ask someone else to choose | Hide it from everyone
test: Mum asks, «Can you specify what time you will be home?» What does she want? | A joke | *An exact time | Dinner at seven | Nothing at all, just a guess
exam: In maths, the question says «specify the units». What must you do? | Draw a fish | Add more numbers | *Say exactly which units, such as cm or kg | Ignore the units
